// "Adapt N" [CR#701.46a] = "If this permanent has no +1/+1 counters on it, put
// N +1/+1 counters on it." The counter test is the whole condition: the rule
// asks only whether any are there, not how many.
KeywordAction(
    name: "adapt",
    params: [Amount],
    spelling: "adapt",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "adapt",
        frame_set: MeasureComplement,
    ),
    body: Enact(
        verb: Action(label: "Adapt"),
        instruction: DoIf(
        condition: Not(condition: Matches(
            subject: AsMarker(marker: Permanent, subject: This),
            predicate: HasCounters(kind: Boost(power: Up(amount: 1), toughness: Up(amount: 1))),
        )),
        instruction: PutCounters(
            amount: Param(0),
            kind: Printed(kind: Boost(power: Up(amount: 1), toughness: Up(amount: 1))),
            on: AsMarker(marker: Permanent, subject: This),
        ),
        otherwise: None,
    ),
        agent: None,
    ),
)
